WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:04.761
Daisy hurried down the street.

2
00:00:04.762 --> 00:00:08.832
"Come on, Kaleem! We need to find the monster."

3
00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:13.948
"Wait," Kaleem said. "Didn't we promise to walk Finn today?"

4
00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:17.337
Daisy stopped, glad he had remembered that.

5
00:00:17.338 --> 00:00:25.904
"Let's go get Finn. Maybe he can help us with this investigation."

6
00:00:25.905 --> 00:00:28.727
They hurried toward Finn's house.

7
00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:33.223
"Are you sure you understood what the animals said, Daisy?" Kaleem asked.

8
00:00:33.224 --> 00:00:37.125
"It sounds like they were describing totally different monsters."

9
00:00:37.126 --> 00:00:40.808
"That's true." Daisy thought for a second.

10
00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:44.039
"One said the monster was shaggy like a bear.

11
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.107
Another said it had a long neck like a snake."

12
00:00:48.108 --> 00:00:54.683
Kaleem nodded. "And it roars and shoots poison from its mouth, and it's as big as a house.

13
00:00:54.684 --> 00:00:59.368
Either the animals saw different things, or it's definitely a monster."

14
00:00:59.369 --> 00:01:04.448
"It's not a monster," Daisy said for what felt like the millionth time.

15
00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:08.000
"But I suppose they could have seen different things."

16
00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:12.712
"The shaggy creature could be a large dog," Kaleem said.

17
00:01:12.713 --> 00:01:16.801
"And the spitting creature could be a kid with a water blaster."

18
00:01:16.802 --> 00:01:21.298
"No," Daisy said. "These animals know what a dog is.

19
00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:24.244
They wouldn't mix up a dog and a monster.

20
00:01:24.245 --> 00:01:34.484
Not even a big, shaggy one."

21
00:01:34.485 --> 00:01:38.993
Soon they were walking down the sidewalk with lively Finn.

22
00:01:38.994 --> 00:01:44.853
"Woof! Woof!" Finn jumped around like he always did.

23
00:01:44.854 --> 00:01:48.385
"There's a monster? Really? That's so cool!

24
00:01:48.386 --> 00:01:53.581
Or maybe it's scary. Or maybe it's cool and scary!"

25
00:01:53.582 --> 00:01:57.064
"Can you help us track it, Finn?" Daisy said.

26
00:01:57.065 --> 00:01:59.212
"You like smelling things, right?"

27
00:01:59.213 --> 00:02:09.120
"Yes! I have the best nose around!" Finn said proudly. They

28
00:02:09.121 --> 00:02:16.827
went back to the spot where the beagle had seen the monster. "Hey,

29
00:02:16.828 --> 00:02:20.791
how's it going?" Finn barked excitedly. "Want

30
00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:22.545
to play with me?" The

31
00:02:22.546 --> 00:02:27.769
beagle was lying under a table. His voice shook nervously. "No,

32
00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:32.479
I'm too scared to play. There's a monster around here!" "Come

33
00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.379
on, Finn," Daisy said. "Let's explore this neighborhood. We

34
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.567
need to find out what's scaring all the animals." "Oh,

35
00:02:40.568 --> 00:02:42.720
right," Finn said. "Don't

36
00:02:42.721 --> 00:02:45.421
worry, buddy," he said to the beagle. "We'll

37
00:02:45.422 --> 00:02:48.334
figure out this mystery." Finn

38
00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:51.741
stuck his nose on the ground and sniffed. His

39
00:02:51.742 --> 00:02:55.479
tail stiffened, and his eyes widened. "Whoa!"

40
00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:01.107
he cried. "I've never smelled anything like this !"

41
00:03:01.108 --> 00:03:06.079
"That's because we've never had a monster around here," the beagle said.

42
00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.181
"I smelled it too. It was like nothing I'd ever smelled either.

43
00:03:11.182 --> 00:03:15.995
And I've smelled a lot of things!"

44
00:03:15.996 --> 00:03:20.039
Daisy told Kaleem what the dogs were saying.

45
00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.448
"Can Finn follow the trail?" Kaleem asked.

46
00:03:24.449 --> 00:03:27.335
"Sure I can!"

47
00:03:27.336 --> 00:03:30.294
Finn rushed forward with his nose to the ground.

48
00:03:30.295 --> 00:03:35.419
Daisy was pulled along by the leash.

49
00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:39.633
"Slow down, Finn!" she called with a laugh.

50
00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:43.863
"I can't run as fast as you can!"

51
00:03:43.864 --> 00:03:55.079
"Sorry." Finn sniffed. "It went this way!"

52
00:03:55.080 --> 00:04:06.700
They followed Finn's nose down the block and around the corner.

53
00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:13.453
The trail kept going.

54
00:04:13.454 --> 00:04:17.579
The houses got farther apart.

55
00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:22.071
Finally Finn's nose led them to a gate.

56
00:04:22.072 --> 00:04:25.739
A sign read Our Little Farm.

57
00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.992
"The smell goes right through the gate."

58
00:04:27.993 --> 00:04:31.468
Finn wagged his tail.

59
00:04:31.469 --> 00:04:35.938
"The monster is at this farm!"

